ction in <italic>Papaver rhoeas</italic>. <source>Plant Cell.</source> <volume>12</volume>:<fpage>1239</fpage>&#x02013;1252.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10899987</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal">Genesca, M., A. Sola, and G. Hotter. <year>2006</year>. Actin cytoskeleton derangement induces apoptosis in renal ischemia/reperfusion. <source>Apoptosis.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>563</fpage>&#x02013;571.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16528472</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal">Gibbon, B.C., D.R. Kovar, and C.J. Staiger. <year>1999</year>. Latrunculin B has different effects on pollen germination and tube growth. <source>Plant Cell.</source> <volume>11</volume>:<fpage>2349</fpage>&#x02013;2364.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10590163</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Gourlay, C.W., and K.R. Ayscough. <year>2005</year>. The actin cytoskeleton: a key regulator of apoptosis and ageing? <source>Nat. Rev. Mol. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>583</fpage>&#x02013;589.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16072039</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Gourlay, C.W., L.N. Carpp, P. Timpson, S.J. Winder, and K.R. Ayscough. <year>2004</year>. A role for the actin cytoskeleton in cell death and aging in yeast. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>164</volume>:<fpage>803</fpage>&#x02013;809.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15024029</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Greenberg, J.T., and N. Yao. <year>2004</year>. The role and regulation of programmed cell death in plant-pathogen interactions. <source>Cell. Microbiol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>201</fpage>&#x02013;211.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14764104</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Huang, S., L. Blanchoin, F. Chaudhry, V.E. Franklin-Tong, and C.J. Staiger. <year>2004</year>. A gelsolin-like